"https://api.github.com/repos/YashNarK/notes/commits/90a21e1c81326a330d546118e1ff163e5887ad7d"}],"sha":"40a01006c9a602a5c7700447fb64bbe2418b9525","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YashNarK/notes/commits/40a01006c9a602a5c7700447fb64bbe2418b9525"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41226521?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/YashNarK","id":41226521,"login":"YashNarK","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMjI2NTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YashNarK/notes/commits/90a21e1c81326a330d546118e1ff163e5887ad7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T14:28:56Z","email":"narenkrithick@gmail.com","name":"YashNarK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T14:28:56Z","email":"narenkrithick@gmail.com","name":"YashNarK"},"message":"Add beginner concepts sections to all 8 React opinion files\n\nEach file now has a top-level ''## Concepts'' section that teaches\nthe fundamentals before introducing any library code.\n\nReact_UI.md:\n- What is a UI Component; the problem with building from scratch\n- The spectrum: Component Libraries, Utility-first, Headless, shadcn\n- Accessibility (a11y) — why and what it means\n- Design Systems — tokens, components, guidelines\n- Decision table: which approach to use when\n\nReact_HTTP.md:\n- What is HTTP; request/response anatomy; status codes\n- REST API conventions (CRUD → HTTP methods)\n- Synchronous vs asynchronous requests\n- The 9 problems with raw fetch in React\n- Transport vs Data Layer (Axios vs TanStack Query)\n- What caching is and why it matters\n\nReact_State.md:\n- What is state; why variables don''t work\n- State vs Props comparison table\n- Immutability and reference equality explained\n- The four kinds of state (local/shared/global/server)\n- The prop-drilling problem with diagram\n\nReact_i18n.md:\n- i18n vs l10n distinction\n- Key vocabulary: locale, translation key, namespace, pluralization\n- The problem with hard-coded strings\n- How translation libraries work (keys → JSON files)\n- Pluralisation rules across languages\n- RTL languages and CSS logical properties\n- Intl API for dates, numbers, currency\n\nReact_Forms.md:\n- What is an HTML form; the form lifecycle (7 steps)\n- Controlled vs Uncontrolled inputs with comparison table\n- What FormData is and how it works\n- Why React forms need extra care (6 problems to solve)\n\nReact_FormValidation.md:\n- What validation is and why it matters\n- Client-side vs server-side validation (can be bypassed!)\n- Validation timing: onChange vs onBlur vs onSubmit\n- Manual if-statements vs schema-based (Zod) comparison\n- What a schema is; error message UX guidelines\n\nReact_DataUpdation.md:\n- What a mutation is (vs a query)\n- CRUD operations with HTTP methods and SQL equivalents\n- PUT vs PATCH distinction\n- The read/write lifecycle (refetch vs cache update)\n- Immutability and reference equality revisited\n- What optimistic updates are and when to use them\n- Update vs refetch vs optimistic decision table\n\nReact_Animations.md:\n- What an animation is (frame-by-frame)\n- CSS transitions vs keyframes vs JS animations\n- The browser rendering pipeline (Layout → Paint → Composite)\n- Cheap vs expensive properties table (transform/opacity = GPU)\n- Easing curves explained with ASCII diagrams\n- Duration-based vs spring-based animation\n- The exit animation problem in React (why CSS alone can''t do it)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6b8f2686c6e0ca06392f707f8ffaa9bf4a35d26f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YashNarK/notes/git/trees/6b8f2686c6e0ca06392f707f8ffaa9bf4a35d26f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YashNarK/notes/git/commits/90a21e1c81326a330d546118e1ff163e5887ad7d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41226521?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/YashNarK","id":41226521,"login":"YashNarK","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMjI2NTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashNarK","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/YashNarK/notes/commit/90a21e1c81326a330d546118e1ff163e5887ad7d","node_id":"C_kwDOKp0b29oAKDkwYTIxZTFjODEzMjZhMzMwZDU0NjExOGUxZmYxNjNlNTg4N2FkN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/YashNarK/notes/commit/355dd4ef447643494998260cf42e7ee92b47e214","sha":"355dd4ef447643494998260cf42e7ee92b47e214","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YashNarK/notes/commits/355dd4ef447643494998260cf42e7ee92b47e214"}],"sha":"90a21e1c